  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Commercial Arithmetic III: hire purchase or a SACCO loan</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 2.4 (d): Compare the total cost of hire purchase with borrowing the cash price from a SACCO at simple interest, and decide which costs less.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 10 (Percentage increase and decrease), Test yourself, question T4 of Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP GCSE Mathematics: Foundation 2 for AQA, Edexcel and OCR two-tier GCSE mathematics, Cambridge University Press, 2007: a credit plan against the cash price; a SACCO loan at simple interest added as a second option, new items and numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
